ext} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437310} :answer-field/id #uuid "24c76314-0f5c-552b-9634-7a579528542d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4afb86c8-970f-594e-bb88-36f6e2c3e725" :question/math-academy-id "q-103233" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cos⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The zeros of the function are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi $\n- **II.** Its graph passes through the point $(0,1)$\n- **III.** The function has maximum values at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The zeros occur at $x=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{2},…,$ which can be written as $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. At $x=0,$ the function has the value $y=cos⁡0=1.$ Therefore, the graph of the function passes through the point $(0,1).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function has a maximum at $x=0,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=2n\\pi .$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176049 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d62743dd-6b08-537d-99a1-950e0129a65b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437312} {:answer/id #uuid "ca6522af-a085-5421-9c2f-2778b4ad8bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca6522af-a085-5421-9c2f-2778b4ad8bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437313} :answer-field/id #uuid "7795f1b0-ab3b-568b-86a9-79ad8f59e765" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62cebc6c-fb9e-5e2f-a4dc-892c8730f19c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437314} {:answer/id #uuid "7c865e34-f1b0-5ac5-896e-1465217ac529" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62cebc6c-fb9e-5e2f-a4dc-892c8730f19c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437314} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a680935-e5c9-5bc1-9251-f1ef3483d3ef" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438686} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1a71c62-3700-5f58-82ca-cdcc35abc891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437316} {:answer/id #uuid "f8103b2e-08e3-58da-8184-32ba8bfa5da1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1a71c62-3700-5f58-82ca-cdcc35abc891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437316} :answer-field/id #uuid "895e53e0-0454-5c88-bc63-752876bb1bff" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2215b590-8140-5323-92bf-8ae24e1b7bb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-103289" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $\n\n- **II.** The function has zeros at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n$\n\n- **III.** The range of the function is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/73/732955302ca49a41f6c43cf242d7c869e630e88d804c4b56a5beb3b081f2d230.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is defined everywhere, except where $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237989 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176049 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36b1a6cb-d9b2-5499-9bed-f6591d1d13f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437318} {:answer/id #uuid "6d863ba2-7deb-5dbd-a418-153187c043da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36b1a6cb-d9b2-5499-9bed-f6591d1d13f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437318} :answer-field/id #uuid "b085e966-e913-5fdf-8891-5d9c59a6837a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438688} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dff2e6d4-d7e6-5cbf-8bd1-6ae518e69246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437320} {:answer/id #uuid "4419d897-28a5-5bc9-9d30-6eda47c75fc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4419d897-28a5-5bc9-9d30-6eda47c75fc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437321} :answer-field/id #uuid "772ee15e-615c-53a7-b9f0-b705e3e4cbdd" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438689} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2a96a27-f532-56b1-b071-6cec50f8503f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437322} {:answer/id #uuid "d47830c6-0653-572d-a8a7-41bbd043f9fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d47830c6-0653-572d-a8a7-41bbd043f9fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437323} :answer-field/id #uuid "98d41179-1f25-5250-b6ec-ea5a42b8c13b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6f5925ee-40c3-50af-9950-ecf1ea188724" :question/math-academy-id "q-103295" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The vertical asymptotes of the function are $x=2n\\pi $\n- **II.** Its graph passes through the point $(0,0)$\n- **III.** $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=tan⁡(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6})$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/c2/c2d0606829588b01f6cba2fa4785b201c47a6d9ffa325d54e64544c9769d7e4a.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the graph of the function passes through the point $(0,0).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi )=tan⁡(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6}).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43695e61-1e83-5a72-9ff3-f9bf8f0ff41d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437324} {:answer/id #uuid "7f9f1b84-1f9d-52ee-b77c-bb7cf2eaf5ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43695e61-1e83-5a72-9ff3-f9bf8f0ff41d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answe