3e1-a6da-d559974acbda" :question/math-academy-id "q-103811" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain of the function is all positive real numbers.\n- **II.** $x=\\frac{9\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n- **III.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-4\\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+6\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The function's domain is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, the statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi $ for any integer $n,$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is false.\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi .$ So, $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-4\\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+6\\pi ).$ Hence, statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9d4f60c-cb6e-5f02-8f4a-a198f7cafa23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437336} {:answer/id #uuid "36efe75c-8338-5448-b8b1-f0f24de49042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9d4f60c-cb6e-5f02-8f4a-a198f7cafa23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437336} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f359a76-6b4d-5ef4-8d92-7e15d488f261" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "434a0e71-1d31-5c13-a968-09b7e4ab49c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437338} {:answer/id #uuid "6e498609-ab5a-526b-bdc2-2b89a7e8bc74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e498609-ab5a-526b-bdc2-2b89a7e8bc74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437339} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3e70be4-e476-5046-a564-3ee1193d0d78" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438698} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85984aac-915a-5905-a791-04f32942b8bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437340} {:answer/id #uuid "4722da66-f024-52e9-b6dc-755aa8810cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4722da66-f024-52e9-b6dc-755aa8810cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437341} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3cd87df-e0b6-57e0-879b-9a26805f19c7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "048ceaff-1e4b-5807-8d50-fab96c1502f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-103814" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$ Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=1$ is the minimum value of the function. $$\n- **II.** $x=9\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n- **III.** The function takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/06/066fe6ce8a65927436d64753ec4e61bfea257405e4b2f81554ac8341572bcf15.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty )$, therefore the function doesn't have a minimum value. Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi $ for any integer $n$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence statement II is true.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$ Hence statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240786 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1d178d2-5151-5b2b-bf3b-a33cca78a0c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437342} {:answer/id #uuid "abb6ef8c-182a-5285-988c-d54db91431a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abb6ef8c-182a-5285-988c-d54db91431a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437343} :answer-field/id #uuid "41be1f60-3f8e-5182-a74a-4843ff7c332a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab6c31ae-d701-59ea-a24e-bccbbbef88f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437344} {:answer/id #uuid "ba6eaced-5a92-52d8-8b9f-4552316e18db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab6c31ae-d701-59ea-a24e-bccbbbef88f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437344} :answer-field/id #uuid "d70122b3-7ecd-576a-83cc-62f210fbd138" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438701} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "502d7dde-403b-5c82-bce4-cc5d707120e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437346} {:answer/id #uuid "43da692e-60dd-5fc5-bc75-f0ee42a60a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "502d7dde-403b-5c82-bce4-cc5d707120e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437346} :answer-field/id #uuid "d72ba1c3-2115-5bb6-b6b6-9c5c9cd843d9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "340a8e11-ca0d-5e08-ab08-b9647c00e4dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-104049" :question/problem "![](images/51/5143df65d0f99c6511dc8ab13262831669c88535e19c986dacdb364e04847f58.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)\\ne f(2)$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. We have $f(2)=2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x) & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}f(x) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=2=f(2).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The graph of the function doesn't have a break at $x=2$ and we can draw the graph of $f(x)$ around $x=2$ without taking our pencil off of the paper."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60efdf1c-df12-5856-aa4c-f4f6fc23d42f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437348} {:answer/id #uuid "cea4be79-bc3f-5364-9f0f-d13cc3390e5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cea4be79-bc3f-5364-9f0f-d13cc3390e5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437349} :answer-field/id #uuid "67208bb7-2119-51cc-97f2-fc43b1d95b36" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438703} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef42aad5-fee8-5449-bbd4-f1ddf4d65e51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437350} {:answer/id #uuid "7f3c2501-c170-5ad7-8f83-f02c8744f9ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef42aad5-fee8-5449-bbd4-f1ddf4d65e51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437350} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f1b2ad2-b8cf-5da8-ab38-a32e460f880a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438704} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e135984-0cd0-5f07-bdfa-2c1791ff56da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437352} {:answer/id #uuid "8ac001f4-ce03-575e-80fe-299ba4a5012e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ac001f4-ce03-575e-80fe-299ba4a5012e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437353} :answer-field/id #uuid "f18fe838-0660-5c6a-8fe2-0675d1705648" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc9393f2-809c-5769-b329-186102da51c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-104051" :question/problem "![](images/65/65b9b32e8fac6a71141ce820855058367e9235129de7334db35a200905474cc0.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x=5$\n\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,5}f(x)$ exists\n\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=5$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $f(5)=2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{5}^{-}}f(x) & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{5}^{+}}f(x) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,  ${lim}_{x\\to \\,5}f(x)$ doesn't exist\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of the function has a jump exactly at $x=5$\nand it's impossible to draw the graph without taking our pencil off of the paper."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240788 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96e53957-3adf-512d-a153-562190ecd98a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437354} {:answer/id #uuid "be515943-b831-586a-a2a6-0858894c576e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be515943-b831-586a-a2a6-0858894c576e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437355} :answer-field/id #uuid "00a7a20b-ccbd-524b-8f79-400afb75fc99" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d596de00-8611-5fa7-8c45-9ce273f5c8b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437356} {:answer/id #uuid "0966841c-0adf-529b-aba1-cb81f9995b41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0966841c-0adf-529b-aba1-cb81f9995b41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437357} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca8755ff-7b6f-5f08-b14f-f993ca66343d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438707} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "838f207e-53e0-52c7-92ca-2adcfd316d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437358} {:answer/id #uuid "17a322fb-de3b-566d-b977-0791a738d3ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "838f207e-53e0-52c7-92ca-2adcfd316d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437358} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd33cb2a-e191-5a12-95bb-03979c786429" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3312f9fe-c2a1-5d75-b752-6c981a0a3f4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-104052" :question/problem "![](images/80/8086893e4587e68f8257b75f2070cf622fa141199d6bd8960f7c4fd8e7bcb349.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is **not** defined at $x=0$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)$ exists\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph we can see that no value has been assigned to $f(x)$ at $x=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x) & =3, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function is not even defined at $x=0.$ The graph contains a break at $x=0.$ It's impossible to draw the graph of $f(x)$ without taking our pencil off of the paper."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240800 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9a2f64f-b3f7-5269-98a9-f17f1936fd6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437360} {:answer/id #uuid "5aba2d92-17d5-581b-ba83-416e31577135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9a2f64f-b3f7-5269-98a9-f17f1936fd6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437360} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4034323-df06-5913-aef3-95acdc3329f0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438709} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd2e9d86-8a7c-5cbe-b475-279c1ac2a7a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437362} {:answer/id #uuid "93a98b73-c51c-50d7-a355-1c0058c19b7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93a98b73-c51c-50d7-a355-1c0058c19b7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437363} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4dd43e3-cfa3-5d79-a551-739b688c4abe" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438710} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c70f8b35-be7c-5f76-ad36-eb2923e9983e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437364} {:answer/id #uuid "1ce5ebea-8788-5a88-b6b5-adf0418527ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ce5ebea-8788-5a88-b6b5-adf0418527ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437365} :answer-field/id #uuid "470e2c3a-d1de-5b69-b0fa-560f0d53fa11" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ad98348d-cbe6-535a-9828-f9008c2ec2e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-104124" :question/problem "![](images/bd/bdcfa35fb04028cbff32992b41214c878443d3815b676a0cf046f5a99bd771bd.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is **not** defined at $x=-2$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}f(x)=f(-2)$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-2$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-2$ and $f(-2)=5.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-{2}^{-}}f(x) & =5, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,-{2}^{+}}f(x) & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}f(x)=5=f(-2).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of $f(x)$ can be drawn without taking our pencil off of the paper in the neighborhood of $x=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240898 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166863 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65adbd80-9647-59d8-bd4a-42f431587c85" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Conservative Vector Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5650cae6-4ebd-5fab-b924-a7307b4e29a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437372} {:answer/id #uuid "6993da07-2440-58cb-93b7-f9bd99118665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6993da07-2440-58cb-93b7-f9bd99118665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437373} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e37b67f-127d-5c2b-b4d2-843eb6fcfe09" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438715} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46b38472-837a-578d-bc86-3da38e6632e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437374} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3efb19-98f5-5322-9115-86ca840350d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca3efb19-98f5-5322-9115-86ca840350d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437375} :answer-field/id #uuid "c18ab833-d485-51f2-bc95-50bb5a8ff3bb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438716} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5941ba21-ceee-5f9b-91b5-ac8cf172b28e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437376} {:answer/id #uuid "15d3424b-50ff-5a9b-a7ba-8a86b14dd910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15d3424b-50ff-5a9b-a7ba-8a86b14dd910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437377} :answer-field/id #uuid "6df86221-3e95-5646-bb83-ccb26044056c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ff94cca-f0c0-5b4f-9e96-5ccdc57e1837" :question/math-academy-id "q-104573" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F=(2x-y)\\,i-x\\,j$\n- **II.** $G=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\,i+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\,j$\n- **III.** $H={e}^{x-y}\\,i-{e}^{x-y}\\,j$" :question/worked-solution "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nNote that for each of our functions, $D={R}^{2}.$ With this in mind, let's check each of the vector fields. \n\n- For the vector field $F,$ we have $P=2x-y$ and $Q=-x.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $G,$ we have $P=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$ and $Q=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy).\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $G$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $H,$ we have $P={e}^{x-y}$ and $Q=-{e}^{x-y}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-{e}^{x-y},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-{e}^{x-y}.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $H$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240901 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166863 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65adbd80-9647-59d8-bd4a-42f431587c85" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Conservative Vector Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65481b7b-861e-5720-a6dd-8d674d4da852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437384} {:answer/id #uuid "cf2c88c4-d301-5e5f-ada9-7861ac00371d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65481b7b-861e-5720-a6dd-8d674d4da852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437384} :answer-field/id #uuid "20435457-d381-5fe1-8f30-f9db1f097122" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438721} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "721521bd-d66b-56ad-b5bc-1f9a532924dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437386} {:answer/id #uuid "3b297167-e02b-58b6-a123-5866263ab82d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b297167-e02b-58b6-a123-5866263ab82d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437387} :answer-field/id #uuid "28606333-ca6f-5543-bf82-4a014fa763e8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438722} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a53745e3-b275-5699-876b-c7e875b44edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437388} {:answer/id #uuid "53a6adf6-bbaa-5c44-b75e-33daf101bb6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53a6adf6-bbaa-5c44-b75e-33daf101bb6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437389} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd839e2a-5adc-5c75-b668-ba299a877b00" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aac0da30-e1e4-5293-838c-ddb161ffe326" :question/math-academy-id "q-104582" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative in their respective domains?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F=(2x-4y)\\,i+(4x-8y)\\,j$\n- **II.** $G={2}^{2x+y+1}\\,i+{2}^{2x+y}\\,j$\n- **III.** $H=2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1)\\,i+\\frac{2{x}^{2}y}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,j$" :question/worked-solution "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nNote that for each of our functions, $D={R}^{2}.$ With this in mind, let's check each of the vector fields.\n\n- For the vector field $F,$ we have $P=2x-4y$ and $Q=4x-8y.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-4,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are not equal, we conclude that $F$ is not conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $G,$ we have $P={2}^{2x+y+1}$ and $Q={2}^{2x+y}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={2}^{2x+y+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={2}^{2x+y+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $G$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $H,$ we have $P=2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1)$ and $Q=\\frac{2{x}^{2}y}{{y}^{2}+1}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{4xy}{{y}^{2}+1},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{4xy}{{y}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $H$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240974 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Divergence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb2fea76-d8f1-5666-a542-917bd5baee71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437390} {:answer/id #uuid "152c789f-5317-52e2-9188-28255c154716" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "152c789f-5317-52e2-9188-28255c154716" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437391} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ac27b51-3d78-5bc3-a8f8-810b27ff1b38" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438724} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3a9ffcb-44f2-5949-95fa-814bfb8cc5a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437392} {:answer/id #uuid "2efd0294-1666-5152-a16a-9dd09a7d9ddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3a9ffcb-44f2-5949-95fa-814bfb8cc5a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437392} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c9e6c62-67a6-523e-b1cd-fd7207ec866b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438725} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8adb53a3-b021-5071-855f-0576c8b568b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437394} {:answer/id #uuid "7405feb1-7683-5595-b311-1a84859ab6ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8adb53a3-b021-5071-855f-0576c8b568b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437394} :answer-field/id #uuid "925b2332-69df-5291-870e-c0a3f090f25c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438726} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7bfa530-747d-5ad6-84ad-036bd0059f0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437396} {:answer/id #uuid "77ab6b50-7aec-5c00-9718-d684cc7f9f64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77ab6b50-7aec-5c00-9718-d684cc7f9f64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437397} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f99b753-4981-57eb-8141-5cc7a73668b9" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438727}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b5e7ba9-0b08-5996-9edf-60b5549da2af" :question/math-academy-id "q-105046" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0bc0e75bb577ca37b89568e14a4e0d03da7ce4f4853c4e8c57d9b2df79897b13.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $∇\\cdot F=0$\n- **II.** $∇\\cdot F>0$\n- **III.** $∇\\cdot F<0$\n- **IV.** $F$ is solenoidal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statements II and III are false. For any point $P,$ the sum of the inward-pointing vectors equals the sum of the outward-pointing vectors. Therefore, $F$ acts neither like a source nor a sink.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere, the vector field $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241079 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Divergence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fc992ec-1afd-513d-b4a8-935bf11a1db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437414} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ae86bd-dc3b-5370-ab3b-9336719bd2c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fc992ec-1afd-513d-b4a8-935bf11a1db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437414} :answer-field/id #uuid "edadb83c-1055-5eb5-a587-5d624186af4e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438736} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3d980f6-7dd1-52ed-9c35-3b5cd4be9f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437416} {:answer/id #uuid "956ccca4-670f-5c14-940c-9c94b57e93ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "956ccca4-670f-5c14-940c-9c94b57e93ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437417} :answer-field/id #uuid "77f0a995-38e4-5d57-8347-383ed693a19a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438737} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfcaf0b4-948d-526a-b01f-36bdeaf81642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437418} {:answer/id #uuid "cd95d5af-5c40-5c79-8812-a19589b0d35d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfcaf0b4-948d-526a-b01f-36bdeaf81642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437418} :answer-field/id #uuid "832e5215-2f00-59ba-acd0-9dda792a61d4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438738} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f3bd3a4-af83-5047-8b63-efebd317e224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437420} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f48472-2cb4-54b3-9e60-7c12a6e8a9b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f3bd3a4-af83-5047-8b63-efebd317e224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437420} :answer-field/id #uuid "98632cbf-edce-5596-bc40-b3809453d48c" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c30bad2f-8979-5b57-acae-23ae1c82d606" :question/math-academy-id "q-105573" :question/problem "![](images/30/3088d088689bbd0dfd33abe8240c6f02cceb257937fc1fccb8ba3df151dbfaab.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{div}\\,F=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{div}\\,F>0$\n- **III.** $\\text{div}\\,F<0$\n- **IV.** $F$ is solenoidal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statements I and III are false. Notice that the lengths of the vector's $y$-components increase as we move vertically away from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241080 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Divergence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3758688-c398-5563-9ef4-6725bb756a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437422} {:answer/id #uuid "20c2906c-786b-5d44-a2ab-80b29dc77300" :answer/type {:d